Ghost Gate -- GHSA-pp4v-v773-9qxg backport

Backport of the upstream security fix "fix(engine)!: reject zero-amount and empty proofs as
resource possession" (upstream commit 965e0bc6f62baba9afef17593aac7b05ab9680e7, GHSA-pp4v-v773-9qxg,
merged 2026-10-01, after the v0.42.0 tag a43773e6 this cohort is pinned to).

A proof created by amount 0, or from an empty set of non-fungible ids, satisfied
rule!(resource(X)) because the requirement check compared only the proofs resource address.
Anyone able to create an empty vault of X could pass any rule gated on holding X: mint, burn,
withdraw, recall, freeze, method rules and OwnerRule::ByAccessRule.

Three hunks: the requirement check skips empty proofs, lock_by_amount refuses a zero amount,
lock_by_non_fungible_ids refuses an empty id set. Proof::is_empty() is the accessor the check uses.
The upstream regression tests are included so the fix is verifiable rather than asserted.

Applying:  git apply -p1 ghsa-empty-proof.patch   (from a clean v0.42.0 checkout)

